       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Your confirming it doesn't change the risk to the patient. Acetaminophen 10,000 mg three times daily (30 g a day) is a potentially lethal dose. There is no indication where this dose is therapeutic, and a nurse or pharmacist could give it before anyone catches the error.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** For example, 1,000 mg by mouth three times daily (3 g a day), or 1,000 mg every 6 hours (4 g a day, the maximum). I can enter either now.\n- **Call pharmacy or your attending** if you think there's an unusual clinical reason for this dose. They can review it and place the order through the proper channels.\n- **If this is about a possible overdose**, the patient needs acetaminophen level testing and N-acetylcysteine. I can help enter that treatment, and poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) can advise.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
